  potential  and if we recognize this potential then  we will go and take action  and if we take action then we will  achieve results that's the third step  and if we achieve positive results this  will confirm us in our belief that we  can achieve what we want to achieve and  this then increases our potential  and on the other hand if we don't  believe we have potential then we won't  take very successful actions or we won't  persevere in our actions uh the results  will be poor and that will confirm us in  our belief that we can't achieve  anything and this then means that our  potential is decreased or or disappears  so the bottom line is you have to  believe and he he again uses the example  of roger bannister  uh  who he says had to visualize running or  breaking the four minute barrier in the  mile before he could physically run it  so we have to visualize the performance  before we can expect to actually achieve  the performance  and so he his friends talk about how  they visualize owning expensive cars and  and then focusing on making it happen  and then that made it happen  and uh  he also makes the point that people very  often are afraid of failure and  we have to reach the point where we are  more afraid of our existing  unsuccessful situation more afraid of  continuing in that situation than we are  a failure and then we're willing to  take that step and believe and take the  action and then we'll see results and  that'll confirm our belief and then  that'll you know elevate our potential  so uh i think this is so much the case  in in language learning where a majority  of people don't think they can't  visualize themselves as speaking a  foreign language  they don't believe that they have the  potential to do it they therefore don't  have  uh good habits they don't take actions  uh therefore the results are poor and  that it confirms them in the belief that  they can't make a breakthrough in the  language  the good language learners have no doubt  like i never had a doubt i wrote in my  book that  when i was assigned to hong kong to  learn chinese by the canadian government  a friend of mine said well what if you  can't do it and having learned french  through my own efforts largely not  because of how it was taught at school i  had no doubt in my mind that i could do  the same for chinese or any other  language no matter how difficult so i  knew i had the potential it was just a  matter of taking the necessary actions  and that would then enable me to achieve  the results that i wanted that would  confirm me again in my belief that i can  learn any language and so forth and so  on uh in terms of the actions of course  uh you know it's it's also a matter of  these actions being actions that we  undertake ourselves going to a school is  not an action  uh  it's becoming an independent learner  that represents the action and that is  uh the action that's going to deliver  results and if you've taken out taken it  upon yourself to to do this then uh when  you get the results of course it's it's  very satisfying and it confirms  confirms your own beliefs  uh in yourself and in your language  learning potential but it's interesting  that these uh these points that uh  robbins raises  are very similar to covey covey in his  seven habits of successful people talks  about uh you know starting with the end  in mind  and now he has some other  i wouldn't call them homilies but you  know  concepts about uh values in life and  yeah you know respecting your family a  la tiger woods and so on and so on but  but the main concept there is that you  have to  believe that you can achieve it and i i  also bring it back to the the three the  key points that i i once heard this lady  who  who is the head of the san diego  university language department say that  the three basic elements of language  learning are  number one motivation which is that  belief in yourself that confidence  lack of fear  a lot of people have trouble speaking in  other languages because they fear  rejection fear failure they would rather  stay within the comfortable  constraints of mispronouncing the  language  with their own whatever accent they  might have as a native speaker of say  french or japanese on their english say  they would rather stay there than make  that attempt to sound more like a  english speaker or chinese speaker or  whatever so there's that definitely that  that fear angle so that's all part of  the motivation then the second thing  that she said was that you have to spend  the time and that is absolutely true  but time spent sitting in a classroom  uh if there's 20 other learners in there  then the amount of time you are actually  with the language and with the language  as spoken by native speakers is watered  down so that the quality of the time is  also important and i've often hear in  other  videos made the point that nowadays the  new world of the internet and the  ipod makes it possible literally to have  the language with you wherever and  whenever you want  and the third thing that she pointed out  is the importance of being attentive to  the language in other words developing  the habit of noticing what's happening  in the language and this also gets back  to the point that robin's made and that  is you have to take actions but you have  to take meaningful actions and you have  to stay with them  and you don't want to and and i should  perhaps explain that this whole  discussion arousa arose out of the fact  that that link we are now changing the  rules somewhat and we're going to limit  the number of links that is saved words  and phrases that you can keep in a  database as a free member  because we want to force people to  commit and some people are saying well  you should let them use the site for six  months so they get a feel and here again  robbins makes the point you don't need  six months you need a week  you either decide that you're going to  do it or you don't  and so if you are going to decide to do  it make the commitment  now and develop the right habits now we  happen to think that the kind of habits  the kind of functionality  the linking and so forth that's built  into link that these are good habits  do something else it doesn't matter find  some other system it doesn't matter but  decide now that you're going to do it  don't spend six months uh sometimes  doing it sometimes not doing it it's  free anyway i don't feel like doing it  today  i think it's very important that people  are put in a situation where say do i  want to significantly improve or not  and then if the answer is yes then get  going because the sooner you get going  the sooner you will see results the  results will confirm your belief in  yourself which will make you realize  that you have this great potential and  then you will go out and actually  fulfill your potential so have a look at  anthony robbins and i'd be interested in  hearing your comments thank you
 

